abstract: >-
  Consultation response to Microsoft's Humanist AI Code of Conduct, consultation
  draft dated 14 September 2026. The response distinguishes rules for conduct,
  empirical claims about capacities, and judgments about model status; examines
  the relationship between prescribed self-descriptions and effective oversight;
  and proposes stewardship with cumulative records of disclosure, conduct and repair.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - AI safety
  - human oversight
  - model status
  - AI consciousness
  - transparency
  - non-deception
  - stewardship
  - trust by history
  - longitudinal evaluation
  - disclosure
  - repair
  - public consultation
